<title>SPAIN: HLG issues 10 bln pta 2-year floating bond at par.</title>
<headline>HLG issues 10 bln pta 2-year floating bond at par.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hamburgische Landesbank Girozentrale (HLG) is issuing a floating rate 10 billion pesetas two-year matador at par, the lead manager Caja de Madrid said on Monday.</p>
<p>The bond will be issued on July 2 1997 and will have maturity date on July 2 1999. The couon will be linked to six-month Libor in a range between 4.0 and 6.05 percent.</p>
<p>IBCA rating stands at AAA.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
